Maintainer: S. Yousaf Ali <yousaf@automatiq.com>
# A Rust toolchain >= 1.88 (rustup) is required as well; Ubuntu's rustc is too
# old, so it is not listed and builds use `dpkg-buildpackage -d`.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), pkg-config, libdbus-1-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/yousafsyed/pocketkey
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: pocketkey
Architecture: amd64
# The window toolkit loads its graphics/display libraries at runtime (dlopen),
# so dpkg-shlibdeps cannot see them; list them explicitly.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, bluez, udev, systemd, acl,
 libxkbcommon0, libegl1, libgl1, libwayland-client0, libwayland-egl1,
 libx11-6, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxrandr2
Recommends: fido2-tools
Description: virtual FIDO2 security key backed by your phone (WebAuthn hybrid)
 pocketkey presents a virtual USB FIDO2 security key to the system via
 /dev/uhid and fulfils CTAP2 requests by proxying them to a phone over the
 WebAuthn hybrid transport (QR code, Bluetooth LE proximity, encrypted
 tunnel). It lets browsers without hybrid support on Linux, such as
 Firefox, use passkeys stored on an Android phone or iPhone.
 .
 A small socket-activated root helper creates the virtual device, so the
 user session never needs access to /dev/uhid.
